{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Only he shall rise</b> — this verse begins with alef and ends with alef: ירפא לו (he shall heal him) — for you, that HaShem sends sufferings upon a person and decrees upon them that they go to that day and that hour." "<b>and acquitted</b> — Three times in the Masorah: ונקה המכה, ונקה האיש מעון, מי שלח ידו במשיח ה' ונקה. Three are pardoned for all their sins: a sick person who recovered, a bridegroom, and a king. אם יקום והתהלך בחוץ — like one who recovered and is acquitted of his sins. ונקה האיש — that is, through his giving her the cup and she dying, and he taking another, and then ונקה האיש מעון. מי שלח ידו במשיח ה' ונקה — that is, a king." "<b>only his rest he shall give</b> — to exclude if he violated the words of the physician."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:13:55.874809941Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}